    "text": "To determine the total number of hours David will spend on his data analytics course, we need to calculate the time spent on classes and homework assignments separately and then sum them up.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total time spent on classes each week:\n- David has 2 three-hour classes each week.\n- David has 1 four-hour class each week.\nSo, the total time spent on classes each week is:\n\\[ 2 \\times 3 + 1 \\times 4 = 6 + 4 = 10 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nNext, we know that David spends 4 hours each week on small group homework assignments. Therefore, the total time spent on homework assignments each week is:\n\\[ 4 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nNow, we can find the total time spent on the course by adding the time spent on classes and the time spent on homework assignments:\n\\[ 10 \\text{ hours} + 4 \\text{ hours} = 14 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nSince the course lasts for 24 weeks, we need to multiply the weekly total by 24 to get the total time spent on the course:\n\\[ 14 \\text{ hours/week} \\times 24 \\text{ weeks} = 336 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of hours David will spend on this course is:\n\\[ \\boxed{336} \\]",
